{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<?ui-args --service-package components/scxml-service-example/package/echo.service.json?>\n<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\"\n       xmlns:env=\"https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env\"\n       version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"s0\">\n  <state id=\"s0\">\n    <invoke type=\"https://stateforward.org/scxml/services/echo\" id=\"echo\" env:tokn=\"API_TOKEN\"/>\n    <transition event=\"echo.fetched\" target=\"done\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"done\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/env001-env-slot-typo.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/env001-env-slot-typo.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":4,"byteOffset":365,"endColumn":83,"endLine":6,"startColumn":79,"startLine":6},"insertedContent":{"text":"token"}}]}],"description":{"text":"bind the declared slot `token`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/env001-env-slot-typo.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":95,"endLine":6,"startColumn":75,"startLine":6}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<invoke>` has no `env` slot `tokn`\n\n**Note:** the package of `https://stateforward.org/scxml/services/echo` declares the slots `endpoint`, `token`\n\n**Help:** did you mean `token`?\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §6.4 <invoke>","text":"`<invoke>` has no `env` slot `tokn`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":381,"start":361},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"ENV001"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"an invoked service's `<invoke>` names the variables whose values its host binds to it with `env:<slot>=\"NAME\"` (or `env:<slot>expr=\"EXPR\"`, an expression that evaluates to the name, evaluated when the `<invoke>` runs) in the `https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env` namespace; the host gives the service component an opaque reference for each slot, for the whole invocation, never the value. The slots an `<invoke>` has are the ones its service package declares (`env-slots`), checked when the validator was given that package; without it (an unbound type, or a `typeexpr`), a slot bound twice (`env:<slot>` and `env:<slot>expr`), an `env:<slot>` value that is not a variable name (`[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*`), or an attribute that names no valid slot (`[a-z][a-z0-9-]*`) is still caught"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: bind only a slot the service's package declares, once, to a variable name.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §6.4 <invoke>\n\nRun `scx --explain ENV001` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#invoke","id":"ENV001","name":"ENV001","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an `env` attribute names a slot its invoked service does not have"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}